{"bdny":{"name":"BDNY 2026","full":"Boutique Design New York","dates":"Sunday November 8 and Monday November 9, 2026","venue":"Javits Center, 429 11th Avenue at 35th Street","url":"bdny.com","exhibitors":861,"note":"861 exhibitors on the a2z floor plan. Most are national and overseas manufacturers with their own sales and finance teams, which is not our buyer. The list below is the New York based, owner led slice worth a booth conversation, plus the three radar firms that are exhibiting.","new":[{"n":"Bokara Rug Company","b":"1268","seg":"Dealers","base":"200 Lexington Avenue, NYDC","grade":"Ideal","loc_ok":false,"why":"Family owned rug house in the New York Design Center. One of a kind inventory, trade pricing, consignment to designers.","open":"Which rugs have been out on approval longer than 60 days, and what is tied up in them."},{"n":"Marc Phillips Decorative Rugs","b":"2425","seg":"Dealers","base":"200 Lexington Avenue, NYDC","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Owner run rug dealer, residential and hospitality, same building as Bokara.","open":"Approval and memo tracking, plus landed cost on imports."},{"n":"Cortina Leathers","b":"2811","seg":"Showrooms","base":"153 West 27th Street, Suite 802","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":true,"why":"Small leather house selling to designers and hotel FF&E. Hides priced by the square foot, lots of custom.","open":"Quote versus invoiced yield on custom hides. Where does the margin leak."},{"n":"P.I.D. Floors","b":"2186","seg":"Kitchens and stone","base":"37 West 20th Street, Flatiron","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":true,"why":"Owner led flooring dealer and installer with a Flatiron showroom. Deposits, installs, punch lists.","open":"Project ledger from deposit to final walk through, same as the stone houses."},{"n":"Mosaique Surface","b":"1156","seg":"Kitchens and stone","base":"200 Lexington Avenue, NYDC","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Boutique mosaic and stone studio, custom orders, overseas fabrication.","open":"Lead time promises versus actual on custom orders."},{"n":"Rug & Kilim","b":"1133","seg":"Dealers","base":"Manhattan, warehouse in New Jersey","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Family rug dealer with thousands of pieces across a gallery and warehouse. Inventory truth is the whole business.","open":"Do the gallery, the warehouse and the website agree on what is in stock."},{"n":"Samuel & Sons Passementerie","b":"2208","seg":"Showrooms","base":"D&D Building, 979 Third Avenue","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Family owned trim house selling through its own showrooms and the trade. Thousands of SKUs, cut yardage.","open":"SKU level margin after cut waste and showroom samples."},{"n":"Zia Priven","b":"2929","seg":"Showrooms","base":"New York, made to order lighting","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Founder led lighting studio, custom fixtures for hotels and residences.","open":"Open orders past promised ship week, in one view."},{"n":"Lib & Co Inc.","b":"873","seg":"Showrooms","base":"New York lighting studio","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Small lighting brand selling to the trade, custom finishes and long lead times.","open":"Deposit exposure on open custom orders."},{"n":"Reid Witlin LTD","b":"255E","seg":"Showrooms","base":"200 Lexington Avenue, NYDC","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Small textile house run by its founder, trade only.","open":"Sample and memo tracking, reorder margin by pattern."},{"n":"Ngala Trading Co.","b":"1146","seg":"Showrooms","base":"200 Lexington Avenue, NYDC","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Founder owned importer of South African lighting and furniture, trade showroom.","open":"Landed cost by container versus quoted price list."},{"n":"ArtStar","b":"1164","seg":"Galleries","base":"New York","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Founder led art curation firm selling limited editions to designers and hotels.","open":"Artist royalty and consignment settlements, edition inventory."},{"n":"DAC Art Consulting","b":"619","seg":"Galleries","base":"New York","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Small art consultancy placing work in hotels and multifamily. Buys on behalf of owners.","open":"Client money out to artists and framers before the owner pays. Deposit exposure."},{"n":"Opiary","b":"137","seg":"Showrooms","base":"Brooklyn","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Small planter and furniture studio, made to order, hospitality clients.","open":"Made to order ledger: capacity, promised dates, deposits."},{"n":"Bespoke Tibetan Carpets","b":"3026","seg":"Dealers","base":"New York","grade":"Strong","loc_ok":false,"why":"Small custom rug studio, every order is a project with an overseas loom.","open":"Order status page the designer can open instead of calling."},{"n":"Architectural Grille","b":"1376","seg":"Showrooms","base":"Brooklyn, family owned since 1945","grade":"Watch","loc_ok":false,"why":"Third generation metal fabricator. Owner led but 50 plus staff and a shop floor, so more operations than boutique.","open":"Quote to ship cycle time and remakes."},{"n":"Innovations","b":"2519","seg":"Showrooms","base":"150 Varick Street","grade":"Watch","loc_ok":false,"why":"Wallcovering house with its own showrooms. Private, mid size, likely has a finance lead.","open":"Only if the owner is in the booth."},{"n":"Infinity Drain","b":"2625","seg":"Showrooms","base":"Amityville, Long Island","grade":"Watch","loc_ok":true,"why":"Family owned manufacturer. Good mindset, but a factory outside Manhattan.","open":"Dealer pricing consistency across reps."},{"n":"Pot \u00e0 Porter","b":"437","seg":"Showrooms","base":"New York","grade":"Watch","loc_ok":false,"why":"Small planter importer. Very small, probably under five people.","open":"Only if they are hiring."},{"n":"ABC Carpet","b":"2324","seg":"Dealers","base":"888 Broadway","grade":"Watch","loc_ok":false,"why":"Iconic store, family owned, but 100 plus staff and a real back office.","open":"Skip unless the conversation finds you."},{"n":"Hudson Valley Lighting Group","b":"2337","seg":"Showrooms","base":"Newburgh, NY","grade":"Pass","loc_ok":false,"why":"300 plus staff, national brands, in house IT.","open":"Skip."},{"n":"Wolf Gordon","b":"555","seg":"Showrooms","base":"Long Island City","grade":"Pass","loc_ok":false,"why":"100 plus staff, ERP in place.","open":"Skip."},{"n":"TileBar","b":"1747","seg":"Kitchens and stone","base":"New York, e-commerce","grade":"Pass","loc_ok":false,"why":"Large online tile retailer with engineering and data teams.","open":"Skip."},{"n":"Waterworks","b":"725","seg":"Showrooms","base":"Danbury, CT with NYC showrooms","grade":"Pass","loc_ok":false,"why":"Corporate, 300 plus staff.","open":"Skip."}],"play":[["Walk the New York cluster first","Bokara 1268, Rug & Kilim 1133, Mosaique 1156, ArtStar 1164, Ngala 1146 and Reid Witlin 255E are within a few aisles of each other in the low numbers. Start there Sunday morning before the hotel buyers arrive."],["Lead with their numbers, not ours","Booth staff want to sell product. Ask the owner question from the card: open orders past promised date, approvals out over 60 days, landed cost versus quote. If the owner is not in the booth, get the owner's name and leave."],["Radar firms are warm calls","Stone Source, Artistic Tile and Nemo are already on the radar with openers. The booth is the easiest version of the walk in: nobody is behind a desk."],["Pass the big brands","Most of the 861 are national manufacturers with finance teams. The Azorian3 filter still applies on the floor: owner led, 5 to 50 people, no data team."],["Follow up Tuesday","Everyone you meet gets the same note Tuesday morning: the one number you asked about and a 20 minute screen share offer on fake data. Log each in the status tracker."]]},"radar":[{"n":"Stone Source","s":"KIT","a":"215 Park Avenue South","h":"Flatiron","w":"stonesource.com","d":"Founder led, Jon Lyons","st":"50 to 150","note":"Stone and tile source for architects, founder led, showrooms in several cities. Spec driven sales with long project cycles.","fix":"Project pipeline from spec to order, quote hit rate and the cost of samples that never convert.","open":"Walk in. Open with spec to order conversion by architect account.","score":81,"grade":"Strong","booth":"2437","ex":"Stone Source","match":"exact"},{"n":"Artistic Tile","s":"KIT","a":"38 West 21st Street","h":"Flatiron","w":"artistictile.com","d":"Family owned, Nancy Epstein founder","st":"150 to 300","note":"Family owned tile and stone house with a Flatiron flagship and several regional showrooms. Many SKUs, imports, slab inventory. Bigger than the sweet spot but still family decided.","fix":"Slab and SKU inventory truth, landed cost, and quote accuracy across showrooms.","open":"Walk in. Open with quote accuracy: how often the installed cost beats the quoted cost and why.","score":73,"grade":"Watch","booth":"2619","ex":"Artistic Tile","match":"exact"},{"n":"Nemo Tile + Stone","s":"KIT","a":"48 East 21st Street","h":"Flatiron","w":"nemotile.com","d":"Family owned, third generation","st":"50 to 150","note":"Family tile business since 1921 with Flatiron and other showrooms, contractor and designer customers. Volume plus custom in the same system.","fix":"Customer master across contractor and designer accounts, pricing control, and inventory by location.","open":"Walk in. Open with pricing control across the showrooms.","score":81,"grade":"Strong","booth":"3037","ex":"Nemo Tile Co.","match":"same company, trade name differs"},{"n":"Matter","s":"SHOW","a":"405 Broome Street","h":"SoHo","w":"mattermatters.com","d":"Jamie Gray, founder","st":"10 to 25","note":"Independent design store and its own Matter Made line. Mix of imported brands and in house production, so landed cost and currency hit every quote.","fix":"Landed cost by vendor and currency, inventory that is really on hand versus on order, and a margin by brand view.","open":"Walk in. Open with landed cost: do quotes still use last year's freight and 